.TH THINKERTOY 1
.SH NAME
thinkertoy \- branching-alternatives tree editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/thinkertoy
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Thinkertoy
is a work-alike of the Thinkertoys/decision-creativity chapter of
Nelson's
.IR "Computer Lib/Dream Machines" :
a tree where each node is a decision, option, or consequence, and its
children are its alternatives or outcomes.
.PP
Nodes are laid out on a canvas and can be dragged anywhere with the
mouse (press, drag, release on a node). The
.B "Add Child"
and
.B "Add Sibling"
buttons add a new node near wherever it was added from, without
disturbing the layout of anything else already placed; the root node
has no siblings. An explicit
.B "Auto Layout"
button is the only operation that recomputes the whole tree's
positions, so a manually arranged layout is never silently discarded
by an unrelated edit.
.PP
Trees are saved as a tab-indented outline, one node per line, with
each node's saved x,y position appended \(em a manually arranged
layout survives save and reload exactly as left. An older file saved
without positions gets one fresh Auto Layout on load instead of
piling every node at the origin.
.PP
If
.I file
is given it is loaded at startup; otherwise a new empty tree (a single
root node) is created.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/thinkertoy.b
